# Copy to .env.local (dev) or set in Hostinger → Node.js app → Environment
# variables (production). Never commit real credentials.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- quote mail
# Two emails go out per instant quote on /quote: the customer's copy of the
# quotation, and the shipping-quote request to the office. Without SMTP_USER
# and SMTP_PASS the route still returns a quote — it just logs the email to the
# server console instead of sending it, and the browser tells the customer so
# and offers WhatsApp/email instead.
#
# Values below are Hostinger's (docs/EMAIL-MIGRATION.md §"Client
# configuration"). Port 465 is implicit TLS; 587 with STARTTLS also works.
# Reminder: the plan caps a mailbox at 100 sends per 24 hours, and this costs
# two per quote — roughly 50 quotes a day.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.hostinger.com
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=admin@tinyhomesa.com
SMTP_PASS=

# Optional. Defaults to "Tiny Homes SA website <SMTP_USER>". Must stay on the
# authenticated mailbox or SPF/DKIM will fail — the customer goes in Reply-To.
# SMTP_FROM="Tiny Homes SA website <admin@tinyhomesa.com>"

# Optional. Where shipping-quote requests land. Defaults to admin@tinyhomesa.com.
# QUOTE_NOTIFY_EMAIL=admin@tinyhomesa.com

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ 3D models
MESHY_API_KEY=
